{"results":[{"url":"https://www.thestandard.com.hk/world/article/142203/Bernie-Sanders-says-Mike-Bloomberg-owns-more-wealth-than-the-bottom-125-million-Americans","final_url":"https://www.thestandard.com.hk/world/article/142203/Bernie-Sanders-says-Mike-Bloomberg-owns-more-wealth-than-the-bottom-125-million-Americans","title":"Bernie Sanders says Mike Bloomberg 'owns more wealth than the bottom 125 million Americans'","description":"Several US Democratic presidential contenders are clashing over whether massive wealth accumulation is un-American or something that should merely be subject to equitable tax rates.Asked about Vermont Senator Bernie Sanders’ tweet that “billionaires should not exist,” Minnesota Senator Amy Klobuchar said during Wednesday’s Democratic debate in Nevada that she supported capitalism but also an appropriate tax rate on wealth, unlike what she felt had been promoted and signed by President Donald Trump.When Sanders argued that billionaires pay an unfairly low tax rate compared to the middle class, former New York City Mayor Mike Bloomberg asked, “Why do you complain? Who","language":"en","text":"INTERNATIONAL\n\nWORLD\n\n# Bernie Sanders says Mike Bloomberg 'owns more wealth than the bottom 125 million Americans'\n\nWORLD\n\n20-02-2020 11:44 HKT\n\nSeveral US Democratic presidential contenders are clashing over whether massive wealth accumulation is un-American or something that should merely be subject to equitable tax rates.\n\nADVERTISEMENT\n\nSCROLL TO CONTINUE WITH CONTENT\n\nAsked about Vermont Senator Bernie Sanders’ tweet that “billionaires should not exist,” Minnesota Senator Amy Klobuchar said during Wednesday’s Democratic debate in Nevada that she supported capitalism but also an appropriate tax rate on wealth, unlike what she felt had been promoted and signed by President Donald Trump.\n\nWhen Sanders argued that billionaires pay an unfairly low tax rate compared to the middle class, former New York City Mayor Mike Bloomberg asked, “Why do you complain? Who wrote the code?”\n\nSanders said the United States has a “grotesque and immoral distribution of wealth and income,” noting that Bloomberg “owns more wealth than the bottom 125 million Americans.”-AP\n\nBillionaire Mike Bloomberg comes under fire at the Democrat debate in Nevada, for amassing wealth.\n\nTop News\n\nCopyright © 2026 The Standard - A division of Sing Tao News Corporation Limited. All rights reserved.","author":"The Standard 英文虎報","published_date":"2020-02-20T11:44:00.000+0800","latency_ms":274.8256360000596,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}